extends base.pug

block title
  title #{T('Code of Conduct')} — #{T('Archivium')}

block doc
  h1 Code of Conduct

  h2 Respectful Communication
  p Engage respectfully with others. Avoid offensive language, harassment, threats, hate speech, or discriminatory behavior. Be constructive in feedback and discussions.

  h2 Collaborative Spirit
  p Respect the contributions of others in collaborative projects. Do not alter or delete shared content without proper authorization.

  h2 Content Integrity
  p Avoid plagiarism, overly explicit content, or content that infringes on others' rights. Ensure all content complies with the following guidelines:
  ul
    li
      b Originality:
      |  All content should be original or properly attributed if based on existing work. Plagiarism is not allowed.
    li
      b Appropriate Content:
      |  Avoid posting grossly explicit, offensive, or illegal content. Content should be suitable for all users of Archivium.
    li
      b Categorization and Tags:
      |  Use appropriate categories and tags to help others find and explore your content.
    li
      b Quality of Contributions:
      |  Strive for clarity and coherence in your public content. Use proper grammar, spelling, and formatting to make your ideas understandable and accessible.
    li
      b No Spam:
      |  Avoid spamming or promoting unrelated content. All content should be relevant to the work in which they are posted.

  h2 Protect Privacy
  p Do not share personal or sensitive information about yourself or others without consent.

  h2 Report Misconduct
  p
    | Report any inappropriate behavior or content to 
    a.link.link-animated(href='mailto:contact@archivium.net') contact@archivium.net
    | .
